  {
   "id": "-qoFC82jBQAJ",
   "from": "Alex Chubaty",
   "author": "71df1ea0682dcc02",
   "date": "2018-09-06T16:03:12Z",
   "subject": "Re: What do I do if I don't want to accept default parameters in wolfAlps module?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">instead of using a list named &quot;parameters&quot;, simply rename it (e.g., myParams) and pass that to the simInit call. `parameters` is a function, so you&#39;re getting a name collision.<div><br></div><div>Alex</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
